course: dictionary
lesson: 3426
title: Words for fire safety
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An extinguisher is a metal container, usually red, that puts out a fire. Its full name is fire extinguisher. «Fire extinguishers use water, foam, powder or carbon dioxide», so the word tells you the job: it puts fire out.
explain: Context clues help here. «Water must never be used on an electrical fire, because water carries electricity» tells you the right extinguisher depends on the fire. The word «never» is a strong clue: it is a rule, not a choice.
explain: The word can also mean something small. A candle snuffer, which puts out a candle flame, is an extinguisher too. Check by swapping your meaning in: "a candle snuffer puts out a light" still makes sense, so you understand it.
explain: Most important: a child should never use an extinguisher. Get out, stay out and call the emergency number: 999 in the UK, 911 in the USA and Canada, 000 in Australia, 111 in New Zealand, or 112 or 999 in Ireland.
fact: An extinguisher is a metal container, usually red, filled with water, foam, powder or gas.
fact: An extinguisher is anything that puts out a fire or a light, such as a candle snuffer.
fact: Water must never be used on an electrical fire, because water carries electricity.
fact: «Carbon dioxide pushes oxygen away from a flame, so poured over a candle it puts it out.»
fact: The coloured band on an extinguisher shows which fires it is for. Children should not use one themselves: get out, stay out and call the emergency number.
exercise: «Fire extinguishers use water, foam, powder or carbon dioxide.» What is a fire extinguisher? | A type of tree found in forests | A loud alarm that rings at school | Unknown | *A metal container, usually red, filled with one of these to put out fire
exercise: Why must water never be used on an electrical fire? | Because electrical fires only need sugar | Because water is too cold to put out fires | Because water is too heavy to carry | *Because water carries electricity
exercise: «Carbon dioxide pushes oxygen away from a flame.» Find and copy one word that means the bright, burning part of a fire. | oxygen | *flame | candle | poured
test: Ben sees a candle snuffer and says it is an extinguisher. Is he right? | No, extinguishers are only for sweets | No, a candle snuffer only lights candles | *Yes, anything that puts out a light can be called an extinguisher | Yes, but only in the kitchen
test: There is a fire at home. What should a child do? | Pour water on the fire | Run back in to fetch the extinguisher | Hide under the bed | *Get out, stay out and call the emergency number
exam: Why is carbon dioxide used in some extinguishers? | It makes the flame grow bigger | *It pushes oxygen away from the flame | It is a cold drink | It carries electricity
